    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Fig 1. Number of patients, number of patient visits, and number of residents per academic year."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 1,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.165, 446.554, 284.192, 469.654 ],
    "font" : "Palatino-Roman",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "percentage of time in clinic for 1-year periods (academic years) for PGY levels ranged from 10% to 30%."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 2,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.165, 303.554, 284.213, 447.654 ],
    "font" : "Palatino-Roman",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Over the 17 years, there were 111 885 visits. After excluding nonresident visits (eg, attending or other professional visits), we counted 79 031 visits that met criteria for our study. Of these visits, 4% (3105) were excluded because the provider could not be clearly identified. There were 75 926 visits left for analyses. The number of patients per year ranged from 751 to 2355 (Fig 1). The number of patient visits per year ranged from 2439 to 6867. Overall and of the visits that qualified for this study, the percentage of visits for WCC was 38% and for sick care was 62%. The percentage of visits for WCC increased from 23% in 1982 to 40% in 1998."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 3,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.165, 226.554, 284.215, 304.654 ],
    "font" : "Palatino-Roman",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Our initial analysis included all visits (sick and well). We found continuity to vary with percentage of time in clinic (Table 1). It was highest (65.3%) when the percentage of time in clinic was 30% (3 half-day sessions per week). There was a significant correlation between continuity and the percentage of time in clinic (r .22, P .01)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 12,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.165, 190.12, 284.214, 208.8 ],
    "font" : "Palatino-Roman",
    "font size" : 8.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "TABLE 1. Percentage of Time in Clinic Versus Continuity Measured by the PHY Formula"
  }, {
